-- title:
--   Open window in a rigidified stratum over an edge chart
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for a fake elliptic curve moduli problem, and the hypotheses come in the following groups.
--
--   **Base rings and Frobenius data.** $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$, and $N$ is a nonzero squarefree natural number divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has cardinality $r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$, and $F_r(x)\equiv x^r \pmod \pi$; thus $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $r$ and $F_r$ lifts its Frobenius. Finally $\mathrm{vdet}$ is a homomorphism $GL_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^n$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^\times$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternionic data.** $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar` (namely $0<a$ or $0<b$, and the completion at a finite place $v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$); $\Lambda$ is a maximal order; $\mu_\Lambda\in\Lambda$ satisfies $\mu_\Lambda^2=-(r\bar r)$ and $\mathrm{star}_\Lambda$ is a map $\Lambda\to\Lambda$ with $\mu_\Lambda\cdot \mathrm{star}_\Lambda(x)=\bar x\,\mu_\Lambda$; $2$ is a unit in $\mathcal O$; and every rational integer lies in $\Lambda$ (hypothesis `hΛℤ`), with `coord` an `IsOrderCoord` presentation of $\Lambda$ by pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ (additive, unital, multiplicative for the $\varpi$-twisted product, injective, dense for every $r$-power precision, and compatible with reduced traces).
--
--   **Moduli schemes over $\mathcal O$.** $\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with its point map $\mathrm{pt}$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ (`IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). For an auxiliary level $n\geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ is a fine moduli space for curves with full level-$n$ structure, carrying a level-twisting action of a group $G$ through $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ (`IsLevelTwistAction`). The forgetful morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ lies over $\mathcal O$, is $G$-invariant, and is compatible with the two point maps. For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with extra level $\ell$, and $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell):\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ are morphisms over $\mathcal O$ computing, on points, the source of an $\ell$-level structure and the target of an $\ell$-level isogeny respectively. Two endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realise, on points, the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$.
--
--   **Definite quaternionic data and the discrete group.** $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; $\Lambda_1$ is maximal, $R_1\subseteq\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$, $n_1$ an adelic unit in the $r$-prime Hecke set of $R_1$ with $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ Eichler of level $Nr$; $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map and $v$ the place over $r$. The subgroup $\Gamma^t$ of units is `awayUnits R₁ v`, and for each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s(\ell)$ and adelic units $s_f(\ell)$ are given with: $s_f(\ell)$ equal to $s(\ell)$ at all places away from $r$ and to $1$ at the places over $r$; the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_f(\ell)^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1,\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1))$ at $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and in the $\ell$-prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}(R_1,n_1)$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}\,s(\ell)=\ell$. The groups $\Gamma^t_\ell$ are $\Gamma^t\cap s(\ell)\Gamma^t s(\ell)^{-1}$, and $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$.
--
--   **The special fibre and its endomorphism dictionary.** $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over that field, $\theta_0$ a system of two-variable formal coordinates for $A_0$, and $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Endomorphisms $e(\gamma),e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ over the base and degrees $\deg(\gamma)$ are given for $\gamma\in\Gamma^t$, subject to: `hE1` (each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure); `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$); `hE1sc` (scalars $\gamma=c$ go to multiplication by $c$ up to powers of $r$); `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ becomes a positive integer multiplication up to $r$-powers then $\gamma$ is a scalar); `hE2` (for every injective embedding into $M_2(K_0)$ of the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and of $\varpi$ in $\operatorname{End}X_0$, there is a single $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a centraliser element whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$); `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ carries a labelling $\mathrm{lab}:\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$, describing the action of $e\gamma$ on $P_0$); `hE4` (over algebraically closed fields above the residue field, every $r$-power-degree level-preserving isogeny pair on a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$ up to $r$-powers); and the group `hE5a`–`hE5e` attached to a further order $R_2\subseteq R_1$ (an order with $r$-power denominators reaching $R_1$) and a family $\hat e$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$: $\hat e$ respects the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level; $\hat e$ is unital, multiplicative and sends integers to multiplications; $\hat e(\bar x)\circ \hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}\,x$; $\hat e$ agrees with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$ up to $r$-powers; and one matrix $g$ simultaneously normalises the images of $\Gamma^t$ and of $R_2$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld moduli package.** $\iota:\mathbb Z_{r^2}\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, $\Phi$ a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$, $MD$ a moduli package over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf, and $\eta$ a map from rigidified objects to $MD$-points satisfying the three clauses of `hη` (on admissible objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies points with isomorphism classes; $\eta$ is compatible with base change; and every $MD$-point is, over the members of a standard open cover, in the image of $\eta$ on admissible objects). $E_0$ is an injective embedding of the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the explicit sense of `hE₀`. The family $e_D$ is, for Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a map from $G$-points of $MD$ to pairs consisting of an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra structure and a Deligne datum, and the hypotheses `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` state that $e_D$ is natural, bijective, has first component the given $\psi$, intertwines the $GL_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points with the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action on Deligne data, and converts $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the first component, $\pi$-translates always existing. The hypothesis `hbdd` provides, for every pair of full lattices $M'\leq M$ in $K_0^2$ with $\pi M\subseteq M'$, a bound $N_\gamma$ such that over Artinian local Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with algebraically closed residue field and $\pi$ nilpotent, any $G$-point whose Deligne datum lies in the edge chart of $(M',M)$ is $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object of index at most $N_\gamma$. Further, $\kappa$ is the residue map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$.** $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$; $A_{0w}$ together with $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ and $k_w$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ of $A_0$ and an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ back to $A_0$ preserving the level, and `hJOINTw` normalises, by one matrix $g$, the images of all $e\gamma$ together with that of $a_w\!\gg\! b_w$, the latter being $r^{k_w}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)g^{-1}$. $\Xi$ assigns to a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ its $\psi$-component is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality for pullbacks of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting a comparison of the auxiliary data up to $r$-powers), and `hΞdef` (an explicit formula: for a curve with formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ there are $j\leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$, transported from $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ at level $j$, admissible for the $(-j)$-twist of $\psi$, and $\Xi$ equals the point built from that twist and $\eta(t)$). A matrix $g_0\in GL_2(K_0)$ is given for which `heqΓ` and `heqW` hold: over connected $B$, translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds to the action of a power of $r$ times $g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $MD$-points, and (when $\bar r$ is invertible) an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ corresponds to the action of a power of $r$ times $g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **The local frame over $C$ and the strata.** $C$ is a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and $\chi_C:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to C$; $PR$ is a functor on $C$-algebras, and $\mathrm{ptR}$ assigns to a full level-$n$ curve over a $C$-algebra $S$ together with a rigidification relative to $\chi_C$ a point of $PR(S)$, subject to `hR2` (naturality under base change compatible with level structures and rigidifications), `hR3s` (every point of $PR(S)$ is of this form), `hR3i` (over connected $S$, equality of two values forces an isomorphism of level structures together with a comparison of rigidifications up to $r$-powers) and `hR1` (the converse implication). A natural transformation $\theta$ from $PR$ to the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ is given, natural in $S$ (`hθnat`) and computing $\theta(\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho))$ as the pullback along $(g_0^{-1})^{-1}$ of the Deligne-datum component of $e_D(\Xi(u,\rho))$ (`hθ`). The map $\mathrm{toM}$ sends points of $PR$ to points of the pullback $M\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}C$, naturally (`hR0`) and compatibly with $\mathrm{ptF}$ (`hR4`). Moreover $PR$ satisfies Zariski descent for standard open covers (`hsh`), unique lifting along square-zero surjections with prescribed image in $M$ (`het'`), and unique lifting along reduction modulo $\pi$ with prescribed image in $M$ (`hred`). Finally, schemes $X_d$ with morphisms $\xi_d:X_d\to M\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}C$, each locally of finite presentation and formally unramified, come with point maps $\mathrm{pts}_d$ to $PR$ and with maps $\mathrm{ptX}_d$ producing $X_d$-points from level-$n$ curves with a rigidification of index exactly $d$ over $\pi$-killed algebras; the hypotheses `hs0`–`hs2`, `hx1`–`hx4` and `hs4` state that any $T$-point of $\xi_d$ forces $\pi=0$ in $T$, that $\mathrm{toM}\circ\mathrm{pts}_d$ is the given point composed with $\xi_d$, that $\mathrm{pts}_d$ is natural, that $\mathrm{pts}_d\circ\mathrm{ptX}_d=\mathrm{ptR}$, that $\mathrm{ptX}_d$ is natural, surjective on $T$-points, and equal on two data exactly when there is an isomorphism of level structures together with a strict comparison of the rigidifications, and that a class $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)$ is in the image of $\mathrm{pts}_d$ exactly when $u$ admits a rigidification of index $d$. Lastly $g_\pi\in GL_2(K_0)$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\gamma\in GL_2(K_0)$ there exist a natural number $D$, a scheme $W$ and a morphism $\iota_W:W\to X_D$ which is an open immersion, such that, writing a $T$-point of $W$ for a section $w$ of $\iota_W\!\gg\!\xi_D\!\gg\!\mathrm{pr}_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}T$, the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, for every Noetherian $C$-algebra and $\mathcal O$-algebra $T$ in a scalar tower over $\mathcal O\to C\to T$ all of whose idempotents are $0$ or $1$, and for any two $T$-points $w,w'$ of $W$, if $\mathrm{pts}_D$ applied to $w$ followed by $\iota_W$ agrees with $\mathrm{pts}_D$ applied to $w'$ followed by $\iota_W$, then $w=w'$.
--
--   Second, for every such $T$ (Noetherian, with the same algebra structures, no connectedness required), every $T$-point $w$ of $W$ and every $x\in PR(T)$ with $\mathrm{pts}_D$ of $w$ followed by $\iota_W$ equal to $x$, the Deligne datum $\theta_T(x)$ lies in the edge chart of the adjacent pair of full lattices $\gamma g_\pi\mathcal O^2\subseteq \gamma\mathcal O^2$; that is, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $T$ the datum is non-degenerate at $\mathfrak p$ along that edge.
--
--   Third, conversely, for every Noetherian local $C$-algebra and $\mathcal O$-algebra $T$ in the same scalar tower in which $\pi$ maps to $0$, and every $x\in PR(T)$ whose datum $\theta_T(x)$ lies in the edge chart of $(\gamma g_\pi\mathcal O^2,\ \gamma\mathcal O^2)$, there is a $T$-point $w$ of $W$ with $\mathrm{pts}_D$ of $w$ followed by $\iota_W$ equal to $x$.
--
--   This is the window step in the chart-by-chart comparison of the rigidified fake-elliptic-curve functor with Drinfeld's formal upper half plane: it isolates inside a single stratum of rigidification index $D$ an open piece on which the point map is injective over connected test algebras and whose image is exactly the locus lying in the edge chart attached to the edge $\gamma(\mathcal O^2 \supseteq g_\pi\mathcal O^2)$ of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $GL_2(K_0)$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_represents_inEdgeChart_of_rigidifiedToG_of_bdd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_represents_inEdgeChart_of_rigidifiedToG_of_bdd), where these windows are glued over the edges of the tree to represent the functor chart by chart.
